# Test Plan

## {{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID}} Test Design

| Test ID | Acceptance ID | Requirement ID | Test implementation | Level | Fixture/data | Expected pre-implementation state | Harness stage |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| TEST-{{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID}}-001 | AC-{{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID}}-001 | REQ-{{REPLACE_ME:CHANGE_ID}}-001 | `path:{{REPLACE_ME:TEST_PATH}}` | `{{REPLACE_ME:TEST_LEVEL}}` | `{{REPLACE_ME:FIXTURE}}` | failing or unsupported: `{{REPLACE_ME:BASELINE_EVIDENCE}}` | `{{REPLACE_ME:STAGE_ID}}` |

### Failure and Boundary Coverage

- `{{REPLACE_ME:FAILURE_PERMISSION_BOUNDARY_CASES}}`

Preserve useful regression tests when requirements change. Add or update tests
linked to the amended acceptance IDs; remove a test only after the requirement
or compatibility promise it protects is formally removed or replaced. Reuse an
existing product stage when it directly proves the criterion, and add a stage
only for a distinct execution boundary. Every listed stage must be scheduled by
committed `HARNESS_VERIFY_STAGES`.

Executable commands and numeric gates remain authoritative only in committed
`HARNESS/config.env`.
